      {
        "id": 239990,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-08-21T22:50:46.447Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thought of another answer I can give to this one.  I am very glad that the character of Muse doesn’t exist in my universe, because I really don’t want a <strong>teenage girl</strong> to go wandering through the dusty back corridors of my mind, discovering my darkest thoughts and then judging me by them.  But I believe that I myself could use such powers in a more responsible fashion, and even if I could only use them on myself, it would be of tremendous benefit to me, being able to invoke my own highest ideals as images so vivid that they grant me a morale bonus to all my actions, or even to confront my fears by manifesting them into tangible forms so that they could be grappled consciously.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
